Subject: [PATCH] extensions: chrome.runtime on web pages from the profile

When the profile sets extensions.externally_connectable, http and https
pages get chrome.runtime and window.browser, as on a real Chrome with a
wallet-style extension installed. file: and about:blank pages get
neither, matching that extension's manifest. When the profile says false
or nothing, the real installed extensions decide, so a real extension's
objects are never withdrawn. The browser process checks each message
against real manifests, so a page learns nothing about what is
installed.

--- a/extensions/renderer/native_extension_bindings_system.cc
+++ b/extensions/renderer/native_extension_bindings_system.cc
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <string_view>
 #include <utility>
 
+#include "base/apostate/profile.h"
 #include "base/command_line.h"
 #include "base/compiler_specific.h"
 #include "base/feature_list.h"
@@ -384,6 +385,34 @@
 // depends on the installed extensions and the active URL (in the case of
 // extensions communicating with external websites).
 bool CanWebpageContextConnectExternally(ScriptContext* context) {
+  // Apostate: a composed identity may answer this question before the host's
+  // extension set does. One boolean is enough because the question is asked
+  // of the whole set at once -- the loop below returns on the first match and
+  // never reports which extension matched -- so a profile that says "some
+  // installed extension names this page in externally_connectable" is
+  // indistinguishable from the set that would have said it.
+  //
+  // The scheme test is the manifest. `externally_connectable.matches` of
+  // ["http://*/*", "https://*/*"] is MetaMask's shape and the one measured
+  // against stock Chrome: every http and https page gets `chrome.runtime` and
+  // `window.browser`, `file://` and `about:blank` get neither. An
+  // unconditional true would instead reproduce an `<all_urls>` manifest,
+  // which is a rarer install and a louder claim.
+  //
+  // Additive, and that is deliberate. nullopt is --fingerprint=host and falls
+  // through. An explicit false also falls through rather than suppressing a
+  // real extension's match: an operator who installed a wallet into this
+  // user-data-dir is already showing the page its content script and its
+  // injected objects, so withdrawing only the runtime accessor would compose
+  // a state no install produces, and the browser process honours the
+  // manifest either way (message_service.cc re-checks
+  // externally_connectable against the source frame's URL and is untouched).
+  const base::apostate::Profile* profile = base::apostate::Profile::Get();
+  if (profile && profile->extensions_externally_connectable().value_or(false) &&
+      context->url().SchemeIsHTTPOrHTTPS()) {
+    return true;
+  }
+
   // TODO(devlin): This doesn't seem thread-safe with ServiceWorkers?
   for (const auto& extension :
        *RendererExtensionRegistry::Get()->GetMainThreadExtensionSet()) {
